Several optional IEs are missing the procedural texts, including:
UE Radio Capability for Paging IE in the INITIAL CONTEXT SETUP REQUEST message;
Default Paging DRX IE in the RAN CONFIGURATION UPDATE message;
Time to Wait IE in the RAN CONFIGURATION UPDATE FAILURE message and AMF CONFIGURATION UPDATE FAILURE message;
UE Presence in Area of Interest List IE in the LOCATION REPORT message;
RAN Node Name IE in the NG SETUP REQUEST message and RAN CONFIGURATION UPDATE message.

In addtion, as described in section 4.1 of TS 38.413, the following procedure specification principles are given. 
Any required inclusion of an optional IE in a response message is explicitly indicated in the procedure text. If the procedure text does not explicitly indicate that an optional IE shall be included in a response message, the optional IE shall not be included

Following the principle above, the optional IEs in the response message should be described clearly. While for IEs in the request message, the procedural texts are needed as well.

